{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794987669,"nonce":"0WaBI0CACs083skyvJ4xo9RQmbU=","title":"[GitHub #81] text_area: double click does not select a word (triple click does not select the line)","message":"Source: https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/issues/81\nReporter: FreeSynergy\nGitHub state at capture: open\nReported: 2026-11-17T00:33:02Z; updated: 2026-11-17T00:33:02Z\nCaptured: 2026-11-18T07:38:25.958Z\n\nStatus: queued from the upstream report. This import does not claim local reproduction, implementation or a fix.\n\nTracking scope and expected outcome\n\nProvide double-click/tap word selection, triple-click logical-line/paragraph selection, and Shift+click anchor extension in text_area. Reuse shared editing behavior where appropriate, cover Unicode word boundaries, and preserve touch/long-press parity. The supplied repro expects selection (0,6)..(0,11) after the second click over world.\n\nOriginal GitHub report\n\n## Summary\n\n`text_input` and `code` select the word under the pointer on double click (via `text_edit::word_at_position`). `text_area` does not: a double click only places the cursor. The source says so (`text_area/handlers.rs`, comment around lines 148-157 on current upstream main: \"text_area doesn't yet implement double-tap word selection\").\n\n## Expected\n\n- Double click selects the word under the pointer.\n- Triple click selects the line (paragraph).\n- Shift+click extends the selection from the anchor.\n- Same for the touch double-tap path, where the long-press timer is currently armed with `None` instead of a word callback.\n\n## Actual\n\nPointer down/up twice at the same spot only sets the cursor; `selection_start` stays `None`, nothing is highlighted.\n\nRepro output (text `\"hello world\\nsecond line\"`, click over \"world\"):\n\n```\nafter click 1: selection_start=None, cursor=(line 0, col 7)\nafter click 2: selection_start=None, cursor=(line 0, col 7)\nafter click 3: selection_start=None, cursor=(line 0, col 7)\n```\nExpected after click 2: selection (0,6)..(0,11).\n\n## Minimal repro\n\n```rust\nuse blinc_core::events::event_types;\nuse blinc_layout::event_handler::EventContext;\nuse blinc_layout::renderer::RenderTree;\nuse blinc_layout::widgets::text_area::{text_area, text_area_state};\n\n#[test]\nfn double_click_selects_nothing() {\n    blinc_theme::ThemeState::init_default();\n    let state = text_area_state();\n    state.lock().unwrap().set_value(\"hello world\\nsecond line\");\n    let area = text_area(\u0026state).w(300.0).rows(4);\n    let mut tree = RenderTree::from_element(\u0026area);\n    tree.compute_layout(400.0, 300.0);\n    let root = tree.root().unwrap();\n    let h = blinc_layout::div::ElementBuilder::event_handlers(\u0026area).unwrap();\n    for _ in 0..2 {\n        for ty in [event_types::POINTER_DOWN, event_types::POINTER_UP] {\n            h.dispatch(\u0026EventContext::new(ty, root)\n                .with_bounds(300.0, 100.0).with_local_pos(70.0, 14.0));\n        }\n    }\n    // inspect state: selection_start (pub(crate)) is None; expected Some((0,6)) with cursor (0,11)\n}\n```\n\n## Environment\n\nBlinc current upstream main. Linux, headless test, default theme.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nMirror the `text_input` pattern: count clicks on the data lock (time and position window), on the second click call `text_edit::word_at_position(line, column)` and set `selection_start`/`cursor`; on the third click select the whole logical line; pass the same closure to `arm_long_press_timer` for touch. For word boundaries, consider Unicode word segmentation (UAX #29, e.g. the `unicode-segmentation` crate) instead of an alphanumeric/space split, so non-Latin scripts and punctuation behave as in other toolkits.\n\nWe are happy to help with a pull request if you tell us which direction you prefer.\n\nAlso tracked in git-bug in our fork FreeSynergy/Blinc (id 433bd1c).","files":null}]}